node_modules
dist
.env

# Raw FIRMS cache and build logs live at the repo root: tens of thousands of
# files, all regenerable. The leading slash matters — without it this would
# also swallow public/data, which holds the built archives we do want.
/data/

# Local tooling output
.wrangler
/shots
*.local

# The global pyramid: a gigabyte of generated binaries, rebuildable from the
# cache by scripts/build-world-*.ts. Git stores each version of a gzipped
# binary whole, so committing it once costs a gigabyte and rebuilding it later
# costs another — the history would grow by the size of the data every time a
# fold changed. The four bundled region cubes stay tracked: they are three
# megabytes and the site is not much without them.
/public/data/world/
